box addthis_default_style element-absent share-links\">\r\n		<a class=\"addthis_button_facebook_like\" fb:like:layout=\"button_count\"></a>\r\n		<a class=\"addthis_button_tweet\"></a>\r\n		<a class=\"addthis_counter addthis_pill_style\"></a>\r\n	</div>\r\n</div>                    </aside>\n                                    </div>\n            </div>\n            \n                        <div class=\"navigation border_radius\" itemscope itemtype=\"http://schema.org/SiteNavigationElement\">\n                <ul id=\"main-menu\" class=\"nav nav-pills\"><li class=\"menu-119 first\"><a href=\"/\" title=\"\">Home</a></li>\n<li class=\"menu-479\"><a href=\"/artistes\">Artistes</a></li>\n<li class=\"menu-370\"><a href=\"/shows\">Shows</a></li>\n<li class=\"menu-123\"><a href=\"/venue\" title=\"\">Venue</a></li>\n<li class=\"menu-255\"><a href=\"/about-us\">About Us</a></li>\n<li class=\"menu-256 last\"><a href=\"/contact-us\">Contact Us</a></li>\n</ul>            </div>\n                    </div>\n    </header>\n\n  <!-- ______________________ MAIN _______________________ -->\n\n  <section class=\"page_holder container\">\n     \n    <div id=\"content-header\">\n      \n              <header class=\"column_title\">\n            <h1 class=\"page_title\">Press Release : Salsa and a touch of London comes to popular Sussex Comedy Club</h1>\n        </header>\n              \n            <div id=\"breadcrumb\" itemprop=\"breadcrumb\">\n          <div class=\"breadcrumb-page column_small\"><a href=\"/\">Home</a></div>      </div>\n         \n      \n              <div class=\"tabs\"></div>\n      \n    </div> <!-- /#content-header -->\n\n    <div class=\"column clearfix\">\n      <div class=\"row-fluid\">\n          <div id=\"main\" class=\"\">\n            <div class=\"region region-content\">\n\n	<div class=\"content\">\n	  <div class=\"block block-system block-odd widget clearfix\">\n                		\n		<div class=\"content\" >\n		  <article class=\"entity entity-press-release press-release-press-release\"  about=\"\" typeof=\"\" itemscope itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Review\" itemprop=\"review\">\n    \n    <div class=\"clearfix column\">\n        <span class=\"white\">Title:</span>\n        <meta itemprop=\"name\" content=\"Salsa and a touch of London comes to popular Sussex Comedy Club\" />\n        <meta itemprop=\"url\" content=\"\" />\n        <div class=\"clearfix column_small\">\n        <ul class=\"act-tags\"><li class=\"act-tag pull-left white\"><a class=\"underline\" href=\"\">Salsa and a touch of London comes to popular Sussex Comedy Club</a></li></ul>        </div>\n    </div>\n    \n    <div class=\"clearfix column\">\n        <span class=\"white\">Press Release For:</span>\n        <div itemprop=\"itemReviewed\" itemscope itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Thing\">\n            <meta itemprop=\"url\" content=\"/shows/26-sept-2014\" />\n            <meta itemprop=\"name\" content=\"Friday, 26th September 2014\" />\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"clearfix column_small\">\n        <ul class=\"act-tags\"><li class=\"act-tag pull-left white\"><a class=\"underline\" href=\"/shows/26-sept-2014\">Friday, 26th September 2014</a></li></ul>        </div>\n    </div>\n    \n        <div class=\"clearfix column\">\n        <span class=\"white\">Press Release Author:</span>\n        <div class=\"clearfix column_small\">\n            <span>Daniel Kington</span>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n        \n        <div class=\"clearfix column\">\n        <span class=\"white\">Press release Date:</span>\n        <div class=\"clearfix column_small\">\n            <span>Sunday, 14 September 2014</span>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n        \n    <div class=\"clearfix column bg-gray padding-20\">\n        <span class=\"white\">Press Release:</span>\n        <div class=\"clearfix column_small white\">\n        <h3>SALSA AND A TOUCH OF LONDON COMES TO POPULAR SUSSEX COMEDY CLUB</h3>\n\n<p>A plethora of talent erupts once again at popular Haywards Heath entertainment venue Danny\'s Comedy Club this month. Another top-drawer line up of comedians has been carefully assembled by the club\'s owner Daniel Kington from acts performing right across the UK.</p>\n\n<p>Spokesperson for the club Mel Sherbourne was quick to point out the pedigrees of those coming to perform at the Birch Hotel on Friday 26th. \"Having become an established venue on the UK comedy scene and with good feedback throughout the industry regarding our audiences and the facilities provided by our hosts at the Birch, we are attracting enquiries from all the serious acts currently performing within the comedy industry.\"</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">Despite the club\'s size precluding for the moment the really top names in British Comedy, Mel explains that there is nevertheless a useful pool of top talent waiting in the wings. \"We only book professional comedians and use those who have supported top names like John Bishop, Alan Carr, Dara O\'Brien and others on tour and we make them our headliners. Last week, we were thrilled when an up-and-coming-act Pierre Novellie, who performed at our first ever show, appeared in a top slot on BBC3\'s primetime Edinburgh Comedy Fest Live. We were totally thrilled.\"</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">This month, Danny\'s Comedy Club welcomes an incredibly likeable and popular talent on the comedy circuit. London-based Sheraz Yousaf draws on his life experiences in a fresh, forthcoming style using humble self-depreciation blended with brilliant comic delivery. During his time on the comedy circuit, Yousaf has performed in all the top clubs such as Jongleurs, The Comedy Store, Laughing Horse, the Komedia and many others.</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">As well as performing live stand-up, Sheraz was also the breakfast radio host on Buzz FM (40k listeners) and was recently filmed for the Laugh Out Loud show on BritAsia TV. One club recently described him thus; \"He manages to draw laughs in so many different ways, hitting you with punchlines from unexpected angles. A good balance of stories and punchlines, with some excellent audience interaction.\" Another said, \"Great stage presence and great material, both us and the audience loved him.\" From others, \"Faultless delivery\" and \"Absolutely brilliant. The crowd loved him.\"</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">Complimenting this month\'s line-up is the hilarious Sonia Aste. Sonia is a witty Spanish comedian who is not afraid to poke fun at other cultures, especially her own. Her comedy is full of sparkling passion and she makes everyone part of the show. her character-driven performance is currently proving a big hit at comedy clubs up and down the country. A recent gig for the Standard Chartered Bank drew the following endorsement; \"... different, fresh, natural and funnily outrageous! It brought loads of laughter and your original improvise interaction with the audience was fantastic!! It takes a lot of creativity, observation and talent to make a group of bankers laugh...\" Sonia has made the finals of a number of prestigious comedy industry awards, taking the Tall Tales Contest at the Actors\' Studio in 2013.</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">Another Edinburgh veteran, Luke Mallison makes a welcome return to the club after an eventful eighteen months. Amongst many others, this up and coming comedian has appeared at The Stand and Komedia. Since performing at Danny\'s first ever show, Mallison has gone on to support comedy star Russell Howard and has performed sketches with BBC Radio Bristol.</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">Sharp, intelligent and very funny, Gabriel Ebulue has been performing for the last five years. His set consists of story-telling, touching on topics including relationships, race, music and his misplaced youth. With his laid back, engaging style, Gabriel has won King Gong at London\'s Comedy Store twice, placed in the finals of The Chortle Student Awards and came second in the prestigious Reading New Act Competition. Most recently, he reached the finals of Up The Creek’s One To Watch Competition. Currently much in demand at the best comedy clubs across London and the south east, he has performed on the same bills as the country’s top comedy acts.</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">Jim Daly is a musical comedian and comedy writer from South London. Revelling in one liners and geeky rapping, he has gigged with big names Doc Brown, Holly Walsh, Sara Pascoe, Kevin Day, Hal Cruttenden, Patrick Monahan and others. Also a finalist for comedy awards, Jim was described by Hal Cruttenden as \"really funny\".</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">\"Former child actor, ex-model and fashion school drop-out,\" London based Joe Sutherland makes his way as a performer, writer and all-round hustler. A caustic, catty and irreverent wit, Joe crafts old-school jokes around the universal subjects of love, sex, death and the rest. He recently made the finals of three prestigious national comedy awards.</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">Mat Wills started his comedy career in March 2011. He quit what he thought was a successful IT career and became an office temp so he could concentrate on writing and performing comedy. According to Mat, \"Classic midlife crisis time!\" He performs 4-6 times a week up and down the comedy clubs and pubs of the UK.</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">Originally a London girl, the hugely popular Haywards Heath singer Cylvian Flynn is a regular star of the Tim French shows on the Boradway and Victoria Park, performing alongside the likes of Katherine Jenkins. Cylvian has fronted several bands as well as solo ventures performing at theatres and music events large and small to great acclaim. Inspired by both Soul and Blues music over many years, she has built a great reputation for bringing sparkle to her performances. Popular and well known on the variety circuit, she has a large and enthusiastic following in Sussex.</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">This month’s show returns to the Birch Hotel, Lewes Road, Haywards Heath on Friday, 26th. Doors open at 7.30 p.m with curtain-up at 8.30. The Club features comfortable, cabaret-style seating, a very reasonably priced bar, good food and ample, free parking onsite. Admission is £7.00 on the door with tickets also available in advance at the Birch Hotel reception.</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">Anyone interested in appearing at Danny’s Comedy Club should email <a href=\"mailto:danny.kington@gmail.com\">danny.kington@gmail.com</a>.</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">For more information, please include the Club’s website: </p><p><a href=\"http://www.dannyscomedyclub.com\">www.dannyscomedyclub.com</a></p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">And links to its Youtube channel: </p>\n<p class=\"column\"><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/user/dannyscomedyclubcom\">http://www.youtube.com/user/dannyscomedyclubcom</a></p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">For further media enquiries, please contact</p>\n\n<p class=\"column\">Danny Kington on <a href=\"07876260506\">0787-626-0506</a> <a href=\"mailto:danny.kington@gmail.com\">danny.kington@gmail.com</a></p>        </div>\n    </div>\n    \n</article>		</div>\n\n</div> <!-- /block -->	</div>\n\n</div> <!-- region -->          </div> <!-- main -->\n                </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- ______________________ FOOTER _______________________ -->\n\n    <footer class=\"footer\" itemscope itemtype=\"http://schema.org/WPFooter\">\n        <div class=\"container\">\n                        <div class=\"clearfix\" itemscope itemtype=\"http://schema.org/SiteNavigationElement\">\n                <ul id=\"secondary-menu\" class=\"align-center unstyled\"><li class=\"menu-257 first last\"><a href=\"/terms-and-conditions\">Terms and Conditions</a></li>\n</ul>            </div>\n                        <div class=\"row-fluid\">\n                <p class=\"span6\">\n                    Copyright &copy; <span itemprop=\"copyrightYear\">2014 </span><span itemprop=\"copyrightHolder\" itemscope itemtype=\"http://schema.org/ComedyClub\"><span i